### 03-01-aq-quality-check.md
[37] sentence: The final questions of Table 3.1 carry every decision of the project, so each must be precise enough to be settled by data.
[38] sentence: The course brief requires every analytical question to be clear, specific, scoped, data-oriented and answerable, and we apply these criteria to the final wording with the following meanings.
[39] sentence: A question is clear when it asks one thing that a reader of the question can restate; specific when it names its measure or target and the groups it compares; scoped when it fixes its population, courses and period; data-oriented when it names the data it needs; and answerable when those data can settle it.

