### 07-00-preparation-pipeline.md
[72] sentence: The data understanding of Section 6 named the issues that could change a conclusion: duplicate click rows, the grain of the click table, missing deprivation bands, activity after withdrawal, the few tasks due by the cut-offs and the narrow population.
[73] sentence: Data preparation turns the seven raw tables into analytic-ready views in which each of those issues is handled by a decision with a reason, and in which no step leaks information from after the moment of prediction.
[74] sentence: Milestone 3 built this pipeline (Milestone 3, Sections 5–7), and the AQ1 and AQ2 analyses of Section 11 and the proposed AQ3 and AQ4 models all read its prepared views.
[75] sentence: The decisions and the pipeline follow; Section 7.1 covers the derived variables, encoding and leakage controls; and Section 7.2 the final prepared dataset, its validation and how it is reproduced.

### 07-01-features-leakage.md
[76] sentence: The pipeline of Section 7 integrates the tables at the enrolment grain; the variables derived from them are what the four questions actually use, and each must be built from information that existed at its cut-off.
[77] sentence: The timing rule, the derived variables, the predictor sets, the encoding and the controls against each form of leakage follow in turn.

### 07-02-prepared-dataset.md
[78] sentence: The decisions of Section 7 and the variables of Section 7.1 produce one versioned prepared dataset, which every analysis of this project reads; it must be shown to change nothing without a rule, to document every column, and to be rebuildable by anyone from the public download.

### 08-00-modeling-strategy.md
[79] sentence: The prepared dataset of Section 7 fixes what each question can use; the modeling strategy fixes how each question is answered, by mapping it to an analytics type, a technical task, a baseline, candidate methods and a primary proposal with its rationale.
[80] sentence: Milestone 4 designed this strategy at Level 1, the compulsory level of the course: methods and their evaluation were specified, and no model was trained (Milestone 4, Sections 2–3).
[81] sentence: In Milestone 5 we ran the descriptive and diagnostic analyses of AQ1 and AQ2 on the 9 runs of 2013 exactly as specified, and Section 11 reports their results; the predictive and ranking questions AQ3 and AQ4 remain proposals, written in the proposal tense, with no model metric.

### 08-01-candidate-methods.md
[82] sentence: The Modeling Briefs of Section 8 fix the technical task of each question; each task now receives the baseline that any method must beat, its candidate methods and a primary proposal with its reason, chosen by criteria rather than by the popularity of an algorithm.
